The entry re-states the parent erdos-214 framework so it stands free of the axiomatized Juhász core:

```lean
abbrev Plane := EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 2)
def IsUnitDistanceFree (S : Set Plane) : Prop :=
  ∀ p q : Plane, p ∈ S → q ∈ S → p ≠ q → dist p q ≠ 1
def ScaledLattice : Set Plane :=
  {p | ∃ a b : ℤ, p 0 = Real.sqrt 2 * a ∧ p 1 = Real.sqrt 2 * b}
```

The parent entry *defines* `ScaledLattice` as a candidate unit-distance-free example but proves nothing about it — leaving Problem #214's hypothesis formally unwitnessed. This entry closes exactly that gap.
